       "evidenceCode": "ECO:0000250",
       "source": "UniProtKB",
       "id": "P63241"
      }
     ],
     "value": "Lys-50 undergoes hypusination, a unique post-translational modification that consists in the addition of a butylamino group from spermidine to lysine side chain, leading to the formation of the unusual amino acid hypusine. eIF-5As are the only known proteins to undergo this modification, which is essential for their function"
